# The allowlist of tools/no-ledger-refs.sh: GLOB REGEX REASON...
* -O[0-3sgz]\b C compiler optimization levels (-O2, -O3)
* U\+[0-9A-Fa-f]{4,6} Unicode code points (U+D800)
runtime/third_party/pcre2/* \b[DFOPQR][0-9]+\b upstream PCRE2 and sljit sources: machine register and opcode-field names (R0, F3, F36) and pattern syntax ((?R0))
runtime/third_party/base64/* \b[DFOPQR][0-9]+\b upstream base64 sources: the assembly macros' register names (R0, R1)
runtime/third_party/yyjson/* \b[DFOPQR][0-9]+\b upstream yyjson source: UTF-8 lead-byte values written as hex (F0, F8)
tools/wave-final.sh LangArena/results/[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[A-Za-z0-9.-]+ a result file of the LangArena repository (its reference timings of the other languages), not a path of the planning notes
bench/valk-gc/* Tables?\sR[1-4](?:\sto\sR[1-4])?\b the rounds tables of bench/valk-gc are named Table R1 to Table R4
* \bR1'(?:\([abc]\))? the young collection's three-way rule, named and defined in runtime/avant_gc.h (with its cases (a) to (c))
compiler/llvm/glue.av default<O[0-3]> LLVM's pass pipeline names (default<O0>, default<O3>)
* D800\sto\sDFFF the UTF-16 surrogate range, named in the lexer's message for \u{...}
tests/cases/test_errors.av \bP(?:2|19)\b struct names of the test programs (P2, P19)
tests/cases/test_gc_typemaps.av \bR[78]\b type names of the test program (records of 7 and 8 reference words)
tests/*ffi/* \b[PQ]2\b C-ABI struct names of the by-value interop fixture (P2, Q2): byval.av, its C side ffi.c, its MIR golden byval.mir
